-- chem/nethop.hypercubical — the concrete hop amplitude of the electron on the diamond net whose every link carries
-- spin ½, from chem/vertexhop.hypercubical. At such a vertex the electron on a link (there of spin 0, the empty link
-- carrying ½ plus the electron's ½ coupled to 0) hops to the neighbour, the link becoming spin 1 (x2 = 1), in two
-- ways by the neighbour's inner label m2 = 0 or 2: the squared amplitudes are 1/4 and 3/4 (`nh-entries`, from
-- chem/bholonomy.hypercubical's `hop-amp` read by chem/linkhop.hypercubical's `lh-read`), summing to 1 (the hop conserves
-- probability, chem/bholonomy's `hop-norm-at` at this vertex, `nh-unit`). So the electron's motion on the net is the
-- walk of chem/cover.hypercubical with amplitude 1 along every link once the link-spin outcome is summed over, and
-- chem/ringmoment.hypercubical's unit-amplitude moments are exactly this motion's. The number multiplying the whole hop
-- is the QSD V matter coupling times ½ℓ_p (the holonomy's edge factor), the single t of chem/ringatom.hypercubical and
-- chem/netatom.hypercubical; it is one number for the whole net, not a free ratio between links, because every link is
-- alike. A leaf: no module imports it.
import "linkhop.hypercubical"

